# Networking Project 

Buy a domain, deploy NGINX on an EC2 instance, and make the page load over your own domain.

# Step 1 - Buy a Domain

I used Cloudflare to buy a domain and my domain is h-abdi.co.uk

# Step 2 - Launch an EC2 instance

I launched my EC2 instance and these were the settings I used for my instance: 

- Instance type = t3.micro
- Created a .pem key
- SSH (22) allowed
- HTTP (80) allowed
- HTTPS (443) allowed

# Step 3 - Connect to the Instance

- My SSH command was : ssh -i ~/Downloads/your-key.pem ubuntu@YOUR_PUBLIC_IP
  
- I had to fix key permissions :  chmod 400 ~/Downloads/h-abdi-key.pem
  
- Then install NGINX : sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y nginx

- Then start NGINX and check it : sudo systemctl enable nginx
sudo systemctl start nginx
sudo systemctl status nginx

- Then tested it works by testing the public IP : http://PUBLIC_IP_ADDRESS

  # STEP 4 - Connect to my domain

- I created two DNS A records in CloudFlare


  # STEP 5 - Test the website

  After creating the two DNS A records it was fully connected and ready to test

  http://www.h-abdi.co.uk and http://h-abdi.co.uk both work

  

